course: dictionary
lesson: 16110
title: Going westwards
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Westwards means towards the west. The west is one of the four main directions, the way the sun sets in the evening. «The birds flew westwards over the sea.» The ending -wards shows movement, so the birds were travelling in the direction of the west.
explain: Break the word into parts: west plus wards. Wards means "in the direction of", so westwards means "west, in the direction of". To check, swap in your meaning: «The birds flew towards the west over the sea» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Maps and weather reports use this word too. «The wind blew westwards all night.» The wind was moving towards the west. When a map is held the normal way up, north is at the top and west is on the left, so westwards means heading left across the map.
fact: Westwards means towards the west.
fact: Westwards is an adverb: it tells you the direction something moves.
fact: Westward means the same thing. It is more common in American English, while westwards is more common in British English.
fact: Phrases you may see in geography: head westwards, move westwards, travel westwards.
fact: «Settlers moved westwards across North America» describes people travelling in the direction of the west.
exercise: «The travellers set off westwards at dawn.» What does westwards mean? | Back home | Towards the north | Very slowly | *Towards the west
exercise: «The ship sailed westwards across the ocean.» Find and copy the word that tells the direction. | *westwards | across | ship | ocean
exercise: «The wind blew westwards.» Which way did the wind move? | Towards the east | *Towards the west | Up into the sky | Towards the south
test: «The geese flew westwards in a long V shape.» What does westwards mean here? | Upwards | Sideways | Towards the east | *Towards the west
test: Which word means towards the west? | Northwards | *Westwards | Eastwards | Downwards
exam: Mia travelled westwards for three days. Which way was she going? | Round in a circle | Towards the north | Towards the east | *Towards the west
